  "id": "BIT-php-min-2025-1218",
  "summary": "Various packet overreads in mysqlnd_writeprotocol.c",
  "details": "The mysqlnd wire protocol parser reads fields out of server packets before checking that the packet still holds enough bytes for them. A malicious or compromised MySQL server can send a truncated packet and make the client read past the end of the packet buffer, which is undefined behaviour and can crash the process.",
